# s17_arch.tkr — §17 `#arch("…")` single-item guard. Two `pick` definitions differ by `#arch`; the
# build-time prune keeps exactly the target's arch, so no duplicate definition survives. On the
# x86_64 host the `#arch("x86_64")` definition survives and `pick` returns 64.

Feature: §17 #arch single-item guard — exactly the target's arch definition survives

  Scenario: x86_64_guard_survives — on x86_64 the #arch("x86_64") pick returns 64, the arm64 one pruned
    When the program is built and run
    Then it exits 64
